## GRADING (binding; the ONE table; capability decides; tier 2, so short)
- **G-1 delta (C1).** A path beyond `DEPLOY.md`, a test, product, package or config byte, or a Route B block byte differing = **Blocker**; a changed line outside main's 218-252, or a main line missing or out of order = **Major, class (d)**; a person's name, real customer name, secret or decision-card slug in an added line or the commit message = **Blocker**; a Jira key, B-number, PR number or percent figure in an added line = **Minor**; non-ASCII, a CR, a tab, a `!` inside double quotes in the added lines, or a line start the readers refuse = **Major**; the words `every pin` or `all pins` as a claim of the paragraph in an added line or the commit message = **Major, class (e)** (C-110 Forbids it); a second commit or a moved head = STOP.
- **G-2 the claims and the census (C2).** A clause no swap turns red on the row it implies, or a clause naming a shape your census finds green = **Major, class (a)**; N3 untrue (an antecedent-true document not red on exactly the 12 rows) or insufficient (a document less red than 12 whose section still holds exactly two fence-shaped lines) = **Major, class (a)**; a sentence false about its own shape (for example the P-H shape, "table row included", "after any white space") = **Major, class (a)** if the clause says "turns a row red" and the shape contradicts it in a document the paragraph describes, **Minor, class (a)** if only a document shape the file does not have contradicts a reading of "sub-section"; a census document red on a row no clause names while the closing sentence stays = **Major, class (b)** (and the closing sentence is the finding); any of the 15 rows red at the head document, or b616 red = **Major, class (c)**; a control among c0, c3, c4, c5 that cannot fail = the run is DEAD (say so, NOT TESTED). The 26 green shapes, the unnamed sibling row 8 pins, the "same path" under-claim and row 15's secondary red = **Notes**.
- **G-3 counts and CI (C3, C4).** The file other than 15 of 15, or b616 off main's count = a finding at the severity of its cause; a third reader of `DEPLOY.md` = STOP; lint, format, typecheck or unit non-zero at the head and zero at main = **Major**; a changed line at or after 473 = **Major**; a failing check-run on the head = **Major**; `in_progress` at the verdict = `CI pending: <names>`, at most GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS (conditional); an open alert on the PR ref = **Blocker** and a STOP; a textual conflict with main = **Major**; a path shared with an open PR = **Major**; a missing PRIOR WORK = returned. **Always Note:** dependabot's vulnerabilities line, the unit chain's one explicit-run skip, the PR body's "Generated with" line.
- **G-4 words (C5, C7).** A commit-message clause: **Major, class (e)** when its behavioural claim is false by a run, **Minor** when it is literally false but its behaviour holds (Tuesday rewrites the squash body). A PR title or body sentence a run does not carry = **Minor** (Tuesday edits it). A builder claim your run contradicts = **Major** if it hides a defect, **Minor** if only a number.
- **G-5 the verdict follows the table, and the cap.** Any Blocker or any Major of the class = `NO GO round 1 of 2`: FOR TUESDAY carries the CLOSED list (with cells), the RESIDUE as ticket text with the tester's cells attached, and the fix shape in prose (one new commit on the same branch; a second NO GO on this class is the cap). Notes and Minors only = `GO` or `GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS`. Add ` (conditional: <reason>)` for any required check not run; `CI pending` is always conditional.

## LOAD (binding; Composer docker route)
8 cores shared with other projects' seats (load1 1.64 at 05:33, 2.41 and 2.69 on the 5 and 15 minute averages). Heavy = `docker build`, any database-test container, any vitest over more than one file, the unit chain, the swap and census loops. **Start a heavy job only while `uptime` load1 is below 7 at two reads 4 s apart** (not independent reads: say so), recorded beside the result; at or over, poll every 20 s, log each wait, do light work meanwhile (C1, the clone, C4 polls, C5/C6/C7 reads). **One heavy job of yours at a time, behind `.tools/b918/lock` AND the project lock above.** A MOVING heartbeat (counter plus `date`) to `.tools/b918/logs/heartbeat.txt` every 30 s from every waiter and long job; a wait loop never uses `pgrep -f` on a pattern in its own command line. Every command gets its input or none (`/dev/null`). NO artificial load. Build `pc-b918-node:head` once from the head's tree: `docker build --pull=false --progress=plain -f <tree>/docker/Dockerfile --target ci -t pc-b918-node:head <tree>` (ABSOLUTE `-f`; `npm ci` must be CACHED); one image serves main and head because the lockfile blobs are equal (prove it by `rev-parse` of the two). **Budget (write it at Step 0, about 11 container starts):** swaps at head 1, swaps at main 1, b778 x3 + TZ 4, b616 1, unit chain 1, prettier 1 (2 at most), controls (scanner, c5) inside the swap loops or 1; image builds 1 (2 at most). Estimated documents: about 99 + 41 + 60 at the head and 99 at main (the head loop is the long one). Remove ONLY your own `pc-b918-*` containers, networks and anonymous postgres volumes, by exact name.

