`psql`, `pg_restore` or the Route B block run end to end; the `packages/db` and `apps/api` groups (only the two files read `DEPLOY.md`, proven at C3); the words' effect on a reader; markdown rendering; a deploy, the demo VM or any hosted host; a locale run; hosted CodeQL beyond the read of the PR's runs; a consistent rename of the `.sql` path in all three lines; the five stale branches (`b61`, `b616`, `b778`, `b806`, `b839`: not open PRs; the builder's PRIOR WORK is a claim); any edit your census does not name.

## HOLDS
Datasec / Security Composer only; if any output shows another client's material, stop and disclose its shape. No deploy, `az`, Kudu, Entra, Graph, ssh. **No HTTP to any hosted or production host or the demo site** (your containers are local). Network: your one in-clone `git fetch`, `gh api -X GET` under the project `GH_CONFIG_DIR`, the in-process Jira GET of C7, cached `docker build` layers, nothing else; `gh run rerun`, `gh workflow run`, `gh pr comment`, `gh pr merge`, `gh pr edit` and any POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE are forbidden; never dismiss an alert. Git in the project repo `2_Project_Files`: READ verbs only (`--no-optional-locks`: ls-remote, log, show, diff, cat-file, ls-tree, rev-parse, rev-list, merge-base, grep, config --get); clone, fetch, worktree add, apply and merge-tree only inside `.tools/b918/repo` and `.tools/wt-b918-*`. **HP-NDA hold:** never open `HP Reporting and Docs/`, any SOW, `1_Project_Definition/Source_Documents/` contents or `inbound/` folders. No Jira write. No decision-queue tool, scoreboard, Artifact, Docs, mail, chat or publish tool. Secrets only as environment; never open `4_Credentials/.env` except the NAME test and the in-process read of the project's Jira client, never `3_Access_Keys/`. **Never delete** (`rm`, `branch -D`, `reset`, `clean`, `stash`, `prune`): quarantine to `.tools/b918/quarantine/`. **Never `cd`**; absolute single-quoted paths (they hold a space and `!`); write `${VAR}:path`; no unquoted word starting with `=` (a separator line is `echo ----`); multi-step chains under `bash -c` or a quoted-heredoc script file (the interactive shell is zsh); `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count; `python3 -I` for anything reading a file you did not write; read your scripts back and scan for non-ASCII (a CR you plant is built at run time with `chr(13)`). Scratch changes live ONLY in `wt-b918-mut`, a container's own layer and `.tools/b918/scratch/`; never in the PR tree. Synthetic data only. No person's name in any id